 ],
 "script": "My furnace just died. In November.\n\nNo problem. I've got home insurance!\n\nHello, insurance? My furnace broke. ... Denied?!\n\nTurns out, home insurance covers sudden disasters. Fire. Storms. A burst pipe.\n\nA furnace that dies of old age? That's wear and tear. Not covered.\n\nAnd a new furnace runs about forty-eight hundred dollars. Ouch.\n\nThat's what a home warranty is for. It covers systems and appliances that wear out.\n\nIt runs about seventy-three dollars a month, plus a service fee per visit. Just read the fine print.\n\nSo. Insurance for disasters. Warranty for breakdowns. Know which one you've got.\n\nIf Homie can figure it out, so can you.",
 "audio_end": 45.205,
